                <pb facs="0409" n="291" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg291"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.5048/51: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wharton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-07-25T12:00:00-00:44">July 25,
                        1929—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 3:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to the Department’s 25, July 23, 6 p.m. Note had been presented by me
                    without change. See my July 24, noon, and July 24, 10 p.m. Liberia awaiting your
                    observations.</p>
                <p>Barclay agrees that you announce at this time that the Liberian Government,
                    disturbed by reports regarding labor conditions in Liberia, are appointing an
                    International Commission to investigate matters on the spot. He adds that he
                    will also make announcement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wharton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
